Synthesis
  14-runner route: the n=14 gate is necessary but seems to create
  leaks; the hardest local example has a long peel rather than a core.
  15-runner route: n=15=3*5 suggests the same CRT-gate descent, now
  with two prime channels; exploratory gated sets also leak.
  Disproof route: sampling tries to maximize coverage under the same
  gates, but no open cover or nonempty protection core appears.
  New common target: prove composite-gate protection cores project to
  smaller Bohr-boundary cores along the n-divisible speed channel.
